   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = 3 \\sqrt{x} - 1 \\). The region R shown is bounded by the graph of f, the line \\( y = -1 \\), and the vertical lines \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( x = 4 \\). Find the exact volume of the solid generated when R is revolved about the line \\( y = -1 \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Multiply",
         [
            "Rational",
            135,
            2
         ],
         "Pi"
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Each slice perpendicular to the x-axis is a disc whose radius is the distance from the curve to the axis, \\( r = f(x) - (-1) = 3 \\sqrt{x} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99058",
         "rule_named": "disc radius"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The volume is \\( \\pi\\int_{1}^{4} \\left(3 \\sqrt{x}\\right)^{2}\\,dx \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "disc method"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( \\int_{1}^{4} 9 x\\,dx = \\frac{135}{2} \\), the volume is \\( \\frac{135 \\pi}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
